<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Privacy manifest. Required at submission since spring 2024.

	Awqat uses location, and NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is still empty. That
	is not an oversight: this key declares data *collected*, meaning
	transmitted off the device. Awqat has no networking code. Prayer times are
	computed on the watch from the coordinates using the solar position
	algorithms in Sources/AwqatCore, which is the whole reason the astronomy
	is implemented here rather than fetched from an API.

	The coordinates are cached in UserDefaults so the app can show times
	before a fix arrives — again, on device only.

	The App Store Connect privacy questionnaire is a separate form and asks a
	different question ("does your app use location?"). Answer yes there, and
	select "not collected" / "not linked to the user" / "not used for
	tracking".

	The purpose string is NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription in
	WatchApp/Info.plist. When-in-use, not always: prayer times need a fix
	occasionally, not a movement history.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
